  "guardrails": [
    "Use the four published category dimensions independently; do not train or optimize toward the external final score or rank.",
    "Freeze SupraCraft automated metrics before comparing them with GDMC human scores.",
    "Treat published human scores as noisy expert/volunteer judgments with judge-preference variance, not canonical truth.",
    "Do not infer causal generator quality from a single cohort or Minecraft version.",
    "Generated maps must be bound to exact downloaded file hashes before running SupraCraft analysis.",
    "Source code and generated-map licenses/redistribution rights must be evaluated separately from public availability.",
    "Do not map GDMC Maintaining Aesthetics to generic beauty; its rubric includes consistency, proportion, appropriate variation and avoidance of jarring procedural artifacts.",
    "Do not map GDMC Functionality to simple mechanical validity; it explicitly includes embodied accessibility, navigation, safety, mob spawning, food/resources, crafting and player-scale affordances."
  ]
